    "turn_text": "Welcome, welcome, welcome to the Fox across America game ball presentation ceremony brought to you each week by the fine folks at Fox across America, where we basically go through the weekend review, you know, you do five of these episodes, they're three hours a day, you have about two guests a day, you're talking about 10 guests for the week, and there's usually one of them I want to highlight because I either had a really, really good time talking to them Or maybe they just kind of gave me some sort of perspective I didn't have prior to the interview. This week's cast did not do that. They underachieved. They were a huge disappointment. I kid I loved all of them. But Wesley Hunt, a representative from the Great State of Texas, the 38th Congressional District of Texas. A black man that is put on the uniform and served this country, also attended West Point. He talked about the state of America in this day and age, where race is constantly weaponized by the left. but results are constantly prioritized by the right. He specifically spoke to the fact that there's a group of young black congressmen that are really changing the political climate in Washington by forcing a substantive conversation around race, as opposed to all the, you know, race baiting that you'd get out of a traditional left-wing pundit class. It was fascinating stuff, but most importantly, it was Wesley Hunt, which is always fun and funny, and there's shots at each other and everything in between. So I am proud, I am proud to consider this our game ball presentation to you. Take the ball and have a great weekend. Hey, hey, hey, it's your radio buddy, Jimmy Phala. And I will tell you this, if I'm searching for my next place to buy, my next place to rent, I just want to scroll through some dream homes. I'm doing it on the Red Fin app. Jenny and I, we get so much entertainment out of this app. I know a lot of people are using it for business and rightfully so. But we will scroll and send each other homes and look at prices and find out everything you need to know. And that's what Redfin is doing. They make it fun to search all the homes for sale, all the apartments for rent in your neighborhood. You can filter for price, beds, baths, square footage, and so much more. And if you find a place you love, Redfin makes it easy to go see it in person, just schedule a tour right from the app. It is that good. Plus, if you look at a cell, Redfin agents know how to get you the best price possible for your home. That's because they close twice as many deals as other agents. And with a listing fee as low as 1%. Redfin's fees are half of what others often charge, which means you'll have more money to put towards your next home. So whether you're looking to buy, rent, or sell, you're just entertaining yourself like me. Redfin's got you covered, download the Redfin app and get started. Jeremy, how are you doing, brother? I'm good. I'm a little bit of a mess right",
